# Archestimator Design System

The app enforces a strict design system via `scripts/enforce-app-design-system.mjs` (run as part of `bun run validate`).

## Tokens

- **Font**: SF Pro, regular/medium weights only
- **Font size**: 12px maximum in the app (landing pages are exempt)
- **Border radius**: xs-only (3px)
- **Letter spacing**: zero
- **Palette**: Neutral (`#292929` / `#5D5D5D` / `#7F7F7F`), custom surface/ink tokens defined in `src/app/globals.css`
- **Icons**: Phosphor Icons (regular weight outline), Lucide (shadcn)

## Component Strategy

Components grow from `src/components/ui/` shared primitives first:
- Button, Badge, Card, Modal, Toast, SearchInput, etc.

Features **must reuse** these rather than creating one-off markup.

## Workshop vs Landing

- **Workshop** (authenticated app): strict 12px max, xs radius, neutral palette enforced
- **Landing pages** (`src/components/landing/` — 32 section components): exempt from in-app size constraint, can use larger typography for marketing

## DESIGN.md Is Alpha-Stage

`DESIGN.md` is **alpha-stage guidance, not law**. Defer to Philip on design decisions. Don't block or revert work on design-system grounds while the visual language is still being developed.

## Storybook

Storybook 10.4 is installed as a **review surface only** — 60+ UI components, 85+ stories. It is NOT a production route. Run `bun run storybook` (port 6006) for review; `bun run storybook:validate` for coverage + boundary + build check.

Don't use Storybook as evidence of production behavior. It's a component review tool.

## Tailwind v4 (CSS-First)

Tailwind CSS v4 uses **CSS-first config** — no `tailwind.config.ts`. Tokens defined in `src/app/globals.css` via `@theme`. Don't add a JS config file.

## Commands

```bash
bun run lint:design-system      # custom design-system enforcement
bun run lint:design             # Impeccable design quality audit (repo-pinned local detector)
bun run storybook               # start Storybook review surface
bun run storybook:validate      # component coverage + boundary + build
```

## Forbidden

- Font sizes > 12px in workshop UI (use design tokens; landing is exempt)
- Border radius > 3px (xs only) in workshop UI
- Non-zero letter-spacing
- Non-SF Pro fonts (without explicit design decision)
- Bold/semibold weights beyond what tokens define (regular/medium only)
- Filled/heavy icon weights (use regular outline)
- One-off markup when a `src/components/ui/` primitive exists
- Adding a `tailwind.config.ts` (Tailwind v4 is CSS-first)

## UI Verification (Proportional)

- **Minor cosmetic** (spacing, copy, color, icon, class tweaks): static review + focused type/LSP/lint is enough
- **Interaction, routing, auth/data state, responsive, a11y**: use browser/Playwright only when the named claim cannot be proved more cheaply
- **Complex composition, CJK text, layout shift**: use visual QA only when pixel evidence is the requested or decisive proof

State the specific browser-only claim before reaching for Playwright. Prefer static, type/LSP, lint, unit, or DOM evidence whenever it proves the same claim.

## Impeccable / visual-qa

Use Impeccable and visual-qa tooling for:

- High-risk UI polish
- Design audits
- Explicit visual-review tasks

Routine UI fixes can lean on `DESIGN.md` and existing component patterns without loading a full design workflow or browser automation.

## Before Adding New Components

1. Check `src/components/ui/` for existing primitive
2. Check `src/components/workshop/` for existing workshop pattern (44+ components)
3. Check Storybook for reviewed variants
4. Only create new if no fit exists AND the new component will be reused

Avoid premature componentization. Inline single-use markup.
